        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Manage Claw MCP server ownership",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- install grouped stdio and remote `sse` / `streamable-http` MCP declarations through the existing validated MCP config writer, including credential-free OAuth intent\n- persist agent/name/digest ownership without storing command arguments, environment references, or other server configuration in the ledger\n- expose MCP ownership and drift in status, round-trip unchanged declarations through export, and remove owned config before cron or agent cleanup\n- preserve pending state when a config write has an unknown outcome and block destructive cleanup until it is reconciled\n\n## Contract\n\n- planning rejects existing global MCP names and apply rechecks atomically with create-only writes\n- removal uses compare-before-unset so operator changes cannot be deleted after planning\n- complete missing and definite-failure references can be safely released; modified and pending references block removal\n- manifest environment values remain unresolved ${ENV_VAR} references and are revalidated during export\n\n## Verification\n\n- pnpm tsgo:core\n- focused Oxlint: 0 warnings, 0 errors across 12 touched files\n- 46 focused MCP/config/add/status/remove/export/CLI tests\n- 8 lifecycle E2E tests, including a real add -> status -> export -> remove MCP config round trip\n\n## Stack\n\n- RFC: https://github.com/openclaw/rfcs/pull/27\n- Depends on: #102383 Gateway cron ownership\n- This PR: validated MCP config and digest-only ownership\n- Next: #102427 projects the complete lifecycle state into doctor diagnostics\n\nMCP is a separate stage because OpenClaw config, rather than the agent entry or Gateway scheduler, owns these declarations. The experimental CLI remains gated by `OPENCLAW_EXPERIMENTAL_CLAWS=1`.",
